# Regenerated by `next dev` and `next build`, and the two write different content
# (.next/dev/types/... versus .next/types/...). Tracked, either form left the tree
# permanently dirty after a build, and update.sh and reset-first-run.sh refuse to
# run against a dirty tree, so a host that had ever built could never be updated.
